%%textfont * 24
%%center Introduction
%%vskip 1cm
%%textfont * 14
%%begintext justify
%%This tune book contains multi-part versions of tunes from Paul Hardy's Session Tunebook,
%%that I have learned to play on my English concertina. Most are traditional tunes from the British Isles.
%%All tunes and arrangements are believed free of current copyright (unless noted explicitly), have permission
%%from the arranger, or else are known or appear to have been placed in the public domain as part of the ongoing
%%live folk music tradition. Please let me know if you are the owner of any that are under access restrictions
%%and I'll remove them.
%%endtext
%%text
%%begintext justify
%%Thanks go to those arrangers who have granted permission for their arrangements to be used, including
%%John McKenzie, Chris Hills, Derek Hobbs, Anahata, and Jennifer Brind. Particular thanks go to Derek Hobbs
%%of Rossleigh Music (https://www.rossleighmusic.com/) for use of some of his accompaniments from the wonderful
%%Piper's Companion series of books, and to Barry Ruffell and the other members of the Rude Mechanicals
%%(http://www.rudemex.co.uk/) who have made available a wealth of arrangements beyond those used here.
%%endtext
%%text
%%begintext justify
%%This tunebook has been prepared using the abcm2ps software, with help from abc2midi, abcmus, Melody Assistant,
%%ABCexplorer, and EasyABC. A big thank you goes to those creative and dedicated people who give their time to
%%create and maintain low-cost or free and open source software for abc music editing and output.
%%endtext
%%text
%%begintext justify
%%The current version of this tunebook, in ABC and in PDF forms, is downloadable for free from
%%Paul's web site at https://pghardy.net, and there you will find the main Paul Hardy's Session Tunebook etc.
%%endtext
